feat(channel,group): implement api runtime bodies

Replace every `todo!()` in `api/channel.rs` and `api/private_group.rs`
with real implementations, the last piece of the shared-runtime refactor.
Until now channel/group worked ONLY through FakeGateway in tests; on
real data `channel_api.send`/`poll`/`leave`/`sendAttachment` and the
equivalent group calls panicked. With these bodies they delegate to the
real runtimes built off the shared Moss node, so the rewritten app
finally drives channel/group on real runtime data.

Each facade mirrors `api/private_dm.rs` exactly (ADR 0016):

- `RUNTIME: OnceLock<Mutex<Option<ChannelRuntime|PrivateGroupRuntime>>>`
  + `LOAD_ERROR` -- the analogue of the Tauri shell's
  `ChannelState`/`PrivateGroupState` (managed struct + `runtime:
  Mutex<Option<...>>` + `load_error`). `ensure_runtime()` is the analogue
  of `*State::ready` (construction) + `with_runtime` (lock + borrow).

- `construct_runtime` borrows the shared resources from
  `api::shared_runtime::ensure_shared_resources()`, builds the runtime
  via `*Runtime::from_shared_node(shared_node, attachment_store,
  persistence)`, then `rehydrate()`. Matches the Tauri shell ordering:
  `ChannelState::ready` (lib.rs L139-160) and
  `PrivateGroupState::ready` (lib.rs L203-224) both called `rehydrate()`
  on construction, so joined channels/groups + their tails + MLS state
  rebuild from the encrypted store after restart.

- Each public fn locks the singleton, drives the `&mut self` runtime
  method, maps `ChannelRuntimeError`/`PrivateGroupError` to a plain
  `String` (ADR 0010). `send_attachment` decodes base64 the same way
  `private_dm::send_attachment` does (the bridge contract for all
  send_attachment facades).

No new tests: the public functions load the live Moss lib via
`ensure_shared_resources`, so a unit test here would need moss.dll
present and fail in CI without it. The DM facade is integration-tested
identically; channel/group get the same treatment in the live-Moss
integration pass. The existing 222 cargo tests + 349 flutter tests pass
unchanged (flutter tests use FakeGateway, not the real bridge).

Verified: cargo test --lib 222/222 (--test-threads=1; two live-Moss
tests are parallel-flaky on the shared identity keystore, pass under
serial), flutter analyze 0 issues, flutter test 349/349.